# AGENTS.md: how to work in this repository

This file is for any AI coding agent (and any human). It is tool-neutral on purpose.
Project: **<%title%>**: <%description%>

## The one rule
**"Done" means `./<%sdlcDir%>/sdlc verify` exits 0 and you can show its report.** Not "the code looks right", not "tests I wrote pass".
The report is `.ai/evidence/latest/report.md`. If you cannot run something, say so; never claim it passed.

## Workflow: PRD -> Code -> Test -> Deploy
| Phase | What you do | Where the procedure lives |
|---|---|---|
| PRD | Write acceptance criteria (`AC-xxx`) and the checks that prove them | `.ai/skills/write-prd/`, `.ai/rules/prd.md` |
<%#hasBackend%>
| Contract | Define the API before code | `.ai/skills/define-contract/`, `.ai/rules/contract.md` |
<%/hasBackend%>
<%#hasDesign%>
| Design | Build screens from the design tokens, every state, then compare with the reference | `.ai/skills/implement-ui/`, `.ai/rules/design.md`, `.ai/design/README.md` |
<%/hasDesign%>
| Code | Small vertical slices, test first | `.ai/skills/implement-feature/`, `.ai/rules/*` |
| Test | Run the loop until green | `.ai/skills/verify-loop/`, `.ai/skills/fix-failing-gate/` |
| Deploy | Tag, let CD promote, verify the live URL | `.ai/skills/release-and-deploy/` |

Start a feature in one of two ways, then run `./<%sdlcDir%>/sdlc implement FEAT-xxx` (the agent writes tests, code, dependencies and config from the spec, and the loop verifies it):
- **From a document:** `./<%sdlcDir%>/sdlc spec requirements.pdf` (also .docx, .md, .txt). An agent drafts `prd.md` and `acceptance.json`, the tool validates them, and **you review the draft** before implementing (skill `.ai/skills/review-spec`).
- **By hand:** `./<%sdlcDir%>/sdlc new <slug>` creates `.ai/specs/FEAT-xxx-<slug>/`; you write `prd.md` and `acceptance.json`.
Worked example: `.ai/specs/FEAT-000-hello-world/`.

## Commands
```bash
./<%sdlcDir%>/sdlc setup      # install dependencies
./<%sdlcDir%>/sdlc doctor     # check the toolchain
./<%sdlcDir%>/sdlc gates      # lint, types, unit tests, build,<%#hasBackend%> contract,<%/hasBackend%> security
./<%sdlcDir%>/sdlc facts      # PRD acceptance criteria vs the RUNNING system (<%runtimeMode%> runtime)
./<%sdlcDir%>/sdlc verify     # gates + facts: exactly what CI runs
./<%sdlcDir%>/sdlc loop       # verify -> heal -> verify (max <%maxIterations%> iterations)
./<%sdlcDir%>/sdlc spec requirements.pdf   # an agent drafts prd.md + acceptance.json from a document; you review the draft
./<%sdlcDir%>/sdlc implement FEAT-001   # spec in (prd.md + acceptance.json), verified code out; needs an agent
./<%sdlcDir%>/sdlc sync       # install dependencies if a manifest (<%manifests%>) changed
<%#hasDesign%>
./<%sdlcDir%>/sdlc design sync    # rewrite the generated files from the design tokens (.ai/design/tokens.json)
./<%sdlcDir%>/sdlc design check   # tokens valid, generated files current, no hard-coded colour, space, radius or font size
<%/hasDesign%>
```
Single gate while iterating: `./<%sdlcDir%>/sdlc gates --only <id>`. `make help` lists the same commands.
On Windows (PowerShell or cmd) the launcher is `.\<%sdlcDir%>\sdlc.cmd`; every command and option is the same. Never edit the launchers (`<%sdlcDir%>/sdlc`, `<%sdlcDir%>/sdlc.cmd`, `<%sdlcDir%>/sdlc.py`).

