## Hard constraints
1. Never edit the machinery that defines "correct": `.ai/sdlc.json`, `<%sdlcDir%>/sdlc*`, `.github/workflows/`. While healing, also never edit `.ai/specs/`. The loop detects this and stops (exit 4).
2. Never delete, skip or weaken a test or a threshold to get green. Fix the code.
<%#hasBackend%>
3. Never change `.ai/contract/openapi.json` to hide drift. It changes only when the PRD changes the API.
4. No secrets in the repo (`./<%sdlcDir%>/sdlc secrets` enforces it). Config comes from environment variables; see `.env.example`.
5. One feature per branch/PR; reference the `FEAT-xxx` id. Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`).
6. If the spec is ambiguous or seems wrong, stop and ask. Do not guess requirements.
<%#hasDesign%>
7. Never hard-code a colour, space, radius or font size in a screen, and never edit a generated tokens file: use the tokens in `.ai/design/tokens.json` (`.ai/rules/design.md`).
<%/hasDesign%>
<%/hasBackend%>
<%^hasBackend%>
